{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39836360",
      "title": "Forwarding Refs to Custom Components",
      "sourceHash": "e07bf46c2a6af687fe0fbf936c16ecebf677e64ffa96f3a2c0177c933da6b1f0",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.75,
          "end": 3.55,
          "en": "So how can we reach out to this dialog",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.186,
          "end": 6.93,
          "en": "from TimerChallenge with help of a ref?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.93,
          "end": 9.84,
          "en": "Well, we can, of course, start by creating a ref here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.84,
          "end": 14.73,
          "en": "in the TimerChallenge component, and I'll name it dialog.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.73,
          "end": 16.43,
          "en": "The name, of course, is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.4,
          "end": 20.91,
          "en": "And now we could, of course, do the following.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.91,
          "end": 24.6,
          "en": "We could go to our ResultModal and add a prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.6,
          "end": 29.34,
          "en": "that could be named ref, though since it's our component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 29.34,
          "end": 31.23,
          "en": "the name, of course, is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.23,
          "end": 34.5,
          "en": "And pass the dialog ref as a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.5,
          "end": 38.433,
          "en": "for this ref prop to our ResultModal component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 40.08,
          "end": 44.04,
          "en": "Inside of that component, we can now destructure it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 44.04,
          "end": 47.88,
          "en": "And now we could try to assign it here as a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 47.88,
          "end": 49.95,
          "en": "for this special ref prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 49.95,
          "end": 52.803,
          "en": "which is supported on all built-in components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 54.48,
          "end": 56.85,
          "en": "So with that, we're in the end forwarding a ref",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 56.85,
          "end": 60.965,
          "en": "that's defined in TimerChallenge, this ref here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 60.965,
          "end": 64.173,
          "en": "to the dialog element in ResultModal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 65.58,
          "end": 68.07,
          "en": "And therefore we should now be able,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 68.07,
          "end": 70.83,
          "en": "here where the timer expired,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 70.83,
          "end": 74.44800000000001,
          "en": "to use this dialog graph and access current,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 74.44800000000001,
          "end": 77.49,
          "en": "which should then hold this dialog element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 77.49,
          "end": 80.727,
          "en": "as a value and call showModal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 83.25,
          "end": 86.37,
          "en": "Because the built-in dialog element has",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 86.37,
          "end": 90.60300000000001,
          "en": "such a showModal method, which you can call to show it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 91.74,
          "end": 94.89,
          "en": "Because as I mentioned before, it's basically invisible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 94.89,
          "end": 97.65,
          "en": "out of the box, but that changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 97.65,
          "end": 100.173,
          "en": "if you call this showModal method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 101.55,
          "end": 103.97999999999999,
          "en": "So that's nothing related to React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 103.97999999999999,
          "end": 107.223,
          "en": "Instead that's a standard browser feature here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 108.53999999999999,
          "end": 112.608,
          "en": "We now just have to make sure that this ResultModal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 112.608,
          "end": 116.64,
          "en": "is always rendered because since it's invisible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 116.64,
          "end": 120.06,
          "en": "and not really part of the visible dom anyways,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 120.06,
          "end": 123.513,
          "en": "having it around like this doesn't cause a problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 125.07,
          "end": 128.01,
          "en": "If we save that and we reload the app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 128.01,
          "end": 130.35,
          "en": "we don't see the dialog.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 130.35,
          "end": 133.68,
          "en": "So having it around all the time isn't a problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 133.68,
          "end": 135.99,
          "en": "And we can now try starting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 135.99,
          "end": 138.12,
          "en": "one of these challenges like the easy one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 138.12,
          "end": 141.72,
          "en": "If I click this, you'll see that after one second,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 141.72,
          "end": 144.963,
          "en": "I indeed do get that modal here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 145.89,
          "end": 150.89,
          "en": "So passing this dialog graph here to ResultModal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 151.26,
          "end": 154.503,
          "en": "and extracting and using it there clearly works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 155.502,
          "end": 160.47,
          "en": "However, this is only the case because this project here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 160.47,
          "end": 164.013,
          "en": "uses at least version React 19.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 164.97,
          "end": 168.96,
          "en": "Prior to that version, so in React projects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 168.96,
          "end": 173.96,
          "en": "that use older React versions, you would've gotten an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 174.48,
          "end": 177.87,
          "en": "Their React would've complained that you can't",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 177.87,
          "end": 180.99,
          "en": "accept a ref like a regular prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 180.99,
          "end": 183.903,
          "en": "This simply didn't work in the past.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 185.01,
          "end": 189.39,
          "en": "And therefore, since my goal with this course, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 189.39,
          "end": 192.69,
          "en": "is to teach you react even if you are using",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 192.69,
          "end": 196.189,
          "en": "a slightly older version, I'll also show you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 196.189,
          "end": 201.15,
          "en": "how you would set up this component to receive a ref",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 201.15,
          "end": 203.43,
          "en": "if you couldn't use this approach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 203.43,
          "end": 206.733,
          "en": "so if you were using an older React version.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 207.57,
          "end": 210.66,
          "en": "Because back then when using an older version,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 210.66,
          "end": 214.89,
          "en": "instead of extracting that ref prop as we just did it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 214.89,
          "end": 219.78,
          "en": "you would've needed to wrap your component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 219.78,
          "end": 222.813,
          "en": "with some function provided by React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 224.589,
          "end": 227.903,
          "en": "So a function that must be imported from React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 229.8,
          "end": 233.76,
          "en": "And that function was called forwardRef,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 233.76,
          "end": 238.38,
          "en": "or is called forwardRef because you can still use it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 238.38,
          "end": 242.463,
          "en": "even if you are using a more modern version of React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 244.08,
          "end": 247.68,
          "en": "This forwardRef function then needs to be wrapped",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 247.68,
          "end": 250.14,
          "en": "around the component function that aims",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 250.14,
          "end": 252.813,
          "en": "to receive and use a ref prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 253.68,
          "end": 254.91,
          "en": "So in this case it's wrapped",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 254.91,
          "end": 256.923,
          "en": "around the ResultModal function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 257.88,
          "end": 261.06,
          "en": "And as a result of calling forwardRef,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 261.06,
          "end": 263.848,
          "en": "you'll get back an adjusted version",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 263.848,
          "end": 267.36,
          "en": "of this component function, you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 267.36,
          "end": 270.3,
          "en": "An adjusted version, which I'll therefore store",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 270.3,
          "end": 272.733,
          "en": "in a constant called ResultModal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 273.57,
          "end": 277.053,
          "en": "So that's now my adjusted component here, so to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 278.01,
          "end": 281.01,
          "en": "And you should then still export",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 281.01,
          "end": 283.92,
          "en": "that adjusted component here to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 283.92,
          "end": 287.013,
          "en": "that it's still available outside of this file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 288.57,
          "end": 293.01,
          "en": "Now with forwardRef wrapped around this component function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 293.01,
          "end": 294.81,
          "en": "this component function then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 294.81,
          "end": 297.75,
          "en": "receives an additional parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 297.75,
          "end": 300.12,
          "en": "So a second parameter besides",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 300.12,
          "end": 302.343,
          "en": "receiving that props parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 303.39,
          "end": 308.39,
          "en": "And that second parameter then is this ref prop, so to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 308.82,
          "end": 311.673,
          "en": "So this special ref prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 313.62,
          "end": 316.86,
          "en": "So whichever value you are setting to the ref prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 316.86,
          "end": 320.61,
          "en": "on your component, in this case this dialog ref,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 320.61,
          "end": 323.61,
          "en": "whatever ref you are setting to this ref prop here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 323.61,
          "end": 326.16,
          "en": "is received as a value through",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 326.16,
          "end": 329.943,
          "en": "that special ref parameter when using forwardRef.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 331.74,
          "end": 335.76,
          "en": "And again, just to be very clear, here in this project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 335.76,
          "end": 339.65999999999997,
          "en": "since we are using a recent version of React here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 339.65999999999997,
          "end": 343.05,
          "en": "forwardRef is not required.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 343.05,
          "end": 345.45,
          "en": "Using it here is optional.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 345.45,
          "end": 348.69,
          "en": "I'm just showing you this syntax here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 348.69,
          "end": 352.62,
          "en": "so that you know about it because you will encounter it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 352.62,
          "end": 356.22,
          "en": "in many projects out there and you will need it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 356.22,
          "end": 360.33,
          "en": "if you are working on some project that might not",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 360.33,
          "end": 363.42,
          "en": "be using the latest React version.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 363.42,
          "end": 367.08,
          "en": "So that's why I will also use this approach here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 367.08,
          "end": 370.32,
          "en": "in this section even though technically here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 370.32,
          "end": 374.88,
          "en": "we don't need it, we could instead just accept and extract",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 374.88,
          "end": 377.7,
          "en": "a ref prop as I showed it to you earlier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 377.7,
          "end": 380.85,
          "en": "and that approach would work just fine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 380.85,
          "end": 382.77,
          "en": "This approach here is optional,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 382.77,
          "end": 386.373,
          "en": "but is required when using an older React version.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}